-- A stray byte in a tag is one token that stops before the first `>`, `/`,
-- `{`, `}`, `"`, `=` or whitespace after it (frontend.md §9.1), so it
-- cannot swallow the tag's own syntax: `\` before `>` and `'s` before `>`
-- are one token each, each tag still ends at its `>`, and each stray is one
-- unexpected_token (8:8, 12:10). The markup is not_implemented at 8:5 and
-- 12:5.
slash =
    <a \> b</a>


quote =
    <a it's>t</a>
